abstract: >
  SAGE implements a selective agentic gating framework for turbofan engine
  Remaining Useful Life (RUL) prediction on NASA CMAPSS FD001. The framework
  combines a lightweight Conv1D-GRU forecaster, a fuzzy D1 confidence gate, a
  numerical Patch Transformer heavy path, and a trained D2 independent verifier
  with confidence-gap decision/fusion. The principal finding is negative:
  selective routing does not improve accuracy because the gate estimates
  small-model error, not the benefit of escalation.
